  "T:excerpt": {
   "x": 43.5,
   "y": 1046.5,
   "w": 440,
   "h": 600,
   "html": "<div class=\"paper excerpt\">\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">It is intriguing to consider the meaning emerging from the integration of these shapes in terms of both their geometric and mathematical relationships. For if we superimpose the three, using the circle as the limiting shape, we discover a very interesting set of relationships (Fig. 2). Given the radius of the circle as unity or one, we find that the edge length of the square within the circle is the square root of two, and that the edge length of the triangle within the circle is the square root of three. The significance of these relationships is that the edge length of the square is precisely the height of a tetrahedron whose base is the same triangle originally circumscribed by the circle (Fig. 3).</p>\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p>\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\"><br></p>\n</div>\n",
   "hide": true,
   "t": 1794062220265
  },
  "NT:mw6is44ez42c": {
   "x": 94.5,
   "y": 963,
   "w": 389,
   "h": 587,
   "html": "<div class=\"paper\">\n<p class=\"pt pt1\" style=\"line-height: 1;\"><br></p>\n<p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">This particular combination of shapes provides all the necessary mathematical information, to transcend from&nbsp; 2-dimensional \"Flatland\", in a world of symbols and shadows.... into the space of 3-dimensional reality, namely in the form of a Tetrahedron, the most primary of space enclosing volumes.&nbsp; This transformation from 2-Dimensions to 3-Dimensions can be thought of as a connective \"bridge\" both abstract and physically real.&nbsp; It is no wonder that these shapes and their relationships have always been considered primary elements in the design and creation of sacred spaces and places. And in fact, the idea that simply conceiving and contemplating the relationships can initiate a change in consciousness.</p><p style=\"font-size: 16px; color: rgb(255, 255, 255);\">To uncover such an elegant connection is to experience delight in the underlying continuity of geometry and the inherent unity of&nbsp; the universe. In contemplating this discovery, one may find profound enlightenment or curious amusement. But certainly, if anything, one must be inspired to look further and to examine other possibilities of connective order and integrated harmony in the transitions between&nbsp; dimensions. If the transcendence between 2-dimensions to 3-dimensions is a matter of the correct relationships and alignments, then perhaps transformations between other dimensions may similarly exist.&nbsp;</p>\n</div>\n",
   "new": "text",
   "t": 1794087741056
  }
 },
